"text": " Barcelona lost a Champions League semi-final because they weren't watching a corner. May 7th, 2019. Anfield. Liverpool had lost the first leg 3-0. And Mohamed Salah and Roberto Firmino were both missing. Divock Origi scored after seven minutes. Then, early in the second half, Jorginho Wijnaldum scored twice in two minutes. Three all on aggregate. 79 minutes, Liverpool win a corner Trent Alexander-Arnold puts the ball down and starts to walk away Barcelona's players turn their backs, they're still getting organised Then he spins round and whips it in Origi is unmarked and fires it in first time 4-0 Liverpool were in the final Less than four weeks later they won it Would you have spotted it? Tell me in the comments",
